WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:01.660
Deep sea.

2
00:00:01.660 --> 00:00:04.360
A monkey on a crocodile's back.

3
00:00:04.360 --> 00:00:06.360
And the crocodile wants his

4
00:00:06.360 --> 00:00:07.170
heart.

5
00:00:07.554 --> 00:00:09.394
The Panchatantra tells this

6
00:00:09.394 --> 00:00:10.954
story. Its teacher,

7
00:00:10.954 --> 00:00:13.634
Vishnusharman, was eighty, and

8
00:00:13.634 --> 00:00:15.254
had six months to make three

9
00:00:15.254 --> 00:00:16.874
bored princes wise.

10
00:00:16.874 --> 00:00:18.964
So he taught with animals.

11
00:00:19.583 --> 00:00:21.463
On the shore of the sea stood

12
00:00:21.463 --> 00:00:24.203
a rose apple tree, never without

13
00:00:24.203 --> 00:00:27.033
fruit. In it lived a monkey.

14
00:00:27.609 --> 00:00:29.789
One day a crocodile crawled out

15
00:00:29.789 --> 00:00:30.429
under it.

16
00:00:30.429 --> 00:00:32.449
The monkey threw him rose

17
00:00:32.449 --> 00:00:34.969
apples, sweet as nectar, and

18
00:00:34.969 --> 00:00:36.359
they became friends.

19
00:00:37.005 --> 00:00:38.925
He took some fruit home to his

20
00:00:38.925 --> 00:00:40.725
wife. Her thought:

21
00:00:40.725 --> 00:00:42.905
whoever eats this daily must

22
00:00:42.905 --> 00:00:44.765
have a heart of nectar.

23
00:00:44.765 --> 00:00:46.735
Bring me that heart.

24
00:00:47.203 --> 00:00:49.663
So he invited his friend home.

25
00:00:49.663 --> 00:00:51.643
Climb on my back.

26
00:00:51.643 --> 00:00:54.423
Far out in deep water, he told

27
00:00:54.423 --> 00:00:55.673
him the plan.

28
00:00:56.215 --> 00:00:58.515
Why didn't you tell me on land?

29
00:00:58.515 --> 00:01:00.235
My sweet heart is in a hole

30
00:01:00.235 --> 00:01:01.225
in the tree!

31
00:01:01.694 --> 00:01:04.534
The crocodile swam happily back.

32
00:01:04.534 --> 00:01:06.674
The monkey ran straight up the

33
00:01:06.674 --> 00:01:07.474
tree.

34
00:01:07.860 --> 00:01:09.080
You fool!

35
00:01:09.080 --> 00:01:11.570
How can anyone have two hearts?

36
00:01:12.005 --> 00:01:14.692
He called it his rebirthday.

37
00:01:16.005 --> 00:01:16.605
For GS4:

38
00:01:16.605 --> 00:01:18.065
presence of mind.

39
00:01:18.065 --> 00:01:21.245
In deep water he did not plead

40
00:01:21.245 --> 00:01:21.925
or panic.

41
00:01:21.925 --> 00:01:24.705
He thought, and found his way

42
00:01:24.705 --> 00:01:25.835
back to land.

43
00:01:26.684 --> 00:01:29.084
One long swim, one quick

44
00:01:29.084 --> 00:01:31.814
thought. Enough to save a life.
